<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<%- include('../partials/sidebar', { activePage: 'tally' }) %>
<div class="main-content">
  <%- include('../partials/header', { pageTitle: 'Tally XML Export Vouchers' }) %>
  <%- include('../partials/alerts') %>
  <div class="content-area" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
    
    <div class="mb-3">
      <a href="/tally/ledger" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Ledgers</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><h3 class="card-title">Download Tally XML Vouchers</h3></div>
      <form action="/tally/export/xml" method="GET" style="padding: 20px;">
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="from-date">From Date *</label>
            <input type="date" name="from" id="from-date" class="form-control" required value="<%= today %>">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="to-date">To Date *</label>
            <input type="date" name="to" id="to-date" class="form-control" required value="<%= today %>">
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="sidebar-divider" style="margin: 20px 0;"></div>
        
        <h4 style="margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight:700;">Account Ledger Mappings (For Tally Sync)</h4>
        <p class="text-secondary fs-sm mb-3">Make sure these ledger names exactly match the ledger names created in your Tally company (case-sensitive) to prevent import errors.</p>
        
        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="sales-ledger">Sales Revenue Ledger Name</label>
          <input type="text" name="sales_ledger" id="sales-ledger" class="form-control" value="Sales Account" placeholder="e.g. Sales Account">
        </div>
        
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="cgst-ledger">CGST Ledger Name</label>
            <input type="text" name="cgst_ledger" id="cgst-ledger" class="form-control" value="CGST Ledger" placeholder="e.g. CGST Ledger">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="sgst-ledger">SGST Ledger Name</label>
            <input type="text" name="sgst_ledger" id="sgst-ledger" class="form-control" value="SGST Ledger" placeholder="e.g. SGST Ledger">
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-block mt-4" style="height: 46px; font-size:16px;">Download Tally Vouchers XML File 📤</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <!-- Instructions Card -->
    <div class="card mt-4" style="padding: 24px;">
      <h3 style="font-weight:700; margin-bottom: 16px;">📖 How to Import XML into TallyPrime / Tally ERP 9</h3>
      <ol style="margin-left: 20px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary);">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Open **Tally** and load your current company account.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Ensure the **Customer Ledgers** (e.g. *Arul Printers*, *Andhra Printers*, etc.) and the **Sales & Tax Ledgers** listed above already exist in Tally.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">From the Gateway of Tally, go to **Import of Data** ➔ **Vouchers**.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Enter the absolute path of the downloaded XML file (e.g. `C:\Users\YourName\Downloads\tally_sales_2026-07-18.xml`).</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Press **Enter** to run the import. Tally will automatically create sales vouchers matching your billing invoices instantly!</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
